{"c":[{"id":"cd83d1662f3b8183","sum":"HI2: Info.plist comment with a double hyphen refuses every build; h1x harness build.sh hardcodes its worktree, cp -cR breaks symlinked node_modules. VS1: Disclosure caps at 8 ways (rebuilt requests need 'plan'); value options state exact outputs (builders.ts optionIs).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c6064da85f9f18d6","sum":"Build gotchas (HI2): a double hyphen in an Info.plist XML comment refuses every build-app.sh mode (the gate parses it); h11/h13/h14 harness build.sh exports from a hardcoded worktree on v2/host and cp -cR turns a symlinked node_modules into a dangling link.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T080815Z-40413337304fea62","text":"The privacy gate parses apps/caret/Bundle/Info.plist as XML, so a double hyphen inside an XML comment refuses every build-app.sh mode (v2/onboard-privacy ccff2558 rewords it; HI2).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T080815Z-5040e69897a0bba9","text":"VM harness build.sh (h11/h13/h14) exports from a hardcoded worktree W, requires the commit on v2/host, and clones W's node_modules with cp -cR, which copies a symlinked node_modules as a dangling link (HI2).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"84a4af324deddcaf","sum":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most 8 ways, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot. Ask value options read 'Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'; stand-ins match them with builders.ts optionIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103634Z-c66a1e426ad50081","text":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason of its parts, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-ffaa923aad520f1c","text":"VS1: an Ask's value options state exact outputs ('Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'); test stand-ins match them with test/builders.ts optionIs, while a fill on focus keeps its quoted-candidate criteria.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ad5eb36f5863fc8a","sum":"Helper tests: generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time; close page sessions before Helper.shutdown. Oracle: realfill-asks seals requests first, so keep oracle rules off FillTrace. Unit-based choices only for Asks naming the source window.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78a720eef0312ba1","sum":"Helper tests: candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time (stats.ms is diagnostic; a cap stop marks a partial window cut); close page sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close, or a trailing walk hits a closed store.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T122806Z-20adf579b39b18f9","text":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time; no setGeneratorClock, budgetMs or --generator-clock override remains. stats.ms is diagnostic, and a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T131449Z-7a0add213d3fc6e0","text":"Tests that wire page sessions into Helper must close those sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close; a scheduled trailing walk otherwise reaches a closed store.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71e3e7853f09b491","sum":"Oracle and choices: realfill-asks seals requests before the canned oracle answers, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there; keep oracle rules off the trace. A source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent, so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T143933Z-2d2e0e57729d25b3","text":"realfill-asks seals each request before the canned oracle answers it, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there: the oracle reads fill questions by their text on the scoreboard but by the trace in the vs1 kit (runB31). Don't make oracle rules depend on the trace.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T143933Z-70fb13e0b1aaff9c","text":"v2/choices: a source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent; a TextEdit note never fits an Ask that does not name it (prose share keeps half back), so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices. The user's request is always a basis.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
